# kbdtap queue: z<id> before the first message after a focus change
tapfocus 4
tappush ca
tappush cb
tapfocus 7
tappush kq
# a too small buffer leaves the message queued
tapread 2
tapread
tapread
tapread
tapread
tapread
# 32 slots: z7 already sent, so 32 pushes fit and the 33rd is full
tappush a
tappush a
tappush a
tappush a
tappush a
tappush a
tappush a
tappush a
tappush a
tappush a
tappush a
tappush a
tappush a
tappush a
tappush a
tappush a
tappush a
tappush a
tappush a
tappush a
tappush a
tappush a
tappush a
tappush a
tappush a
tappush a
tappush a
tappush a
tappush a
tappush a
tappush a
tappush a
tappush a
# a focus change with one free slot: z9 takes it and b, a plain message, is dropped
tapread
tapfocus 9
tappush b
tapread
tapread
# write-back
tapsplit 636100636200
tapsplit 7a3400636100
tapsplit 63
tapsplit 00636100
